  "behavior": [
    "Explicit initialized scratch is included in exact retained capacity; begin_insert validates staged geometry before writing.",
    "Incremental guards require exactly the declared word count. Overlong/failed writes are sticky and clear prior scratch; incomplete/drop/unwind/duplicate/rejected finishes clear staging without changing committed entries.",
    "Completed encodings are hashed contiguously. Duplicate lookup precedes unique-entry allowance checks; successful new entries publish those same staged words without another payload copy.",
    "Persistent owner active flag fences all subsequent mutations after mem::forget(guard); read-only committed lookup remains valid and no recovery/Clone/raw mutable escape is exposed.",
    "One private expression encoder serves ordinary infallible arena insertion, checked nonallocating word counting and the fallible prepared writer.",
    "Encoding preserves tags/flags/byte layout/padding and returns raw table-local u32 ids without implying reserved ExprSet ids, valid children or rebased references.",
    "Typed ExprEncodingError retains storage error source; invalid ByteConcat length rejects before starting the writer."
  ],
